WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.609
Dear Sir or Madam,

00:00:01.859 --> 00:00:13.144
I have been a French teacher at a secondary school for twenty years and I read your article on banning mobile phones at school with interest. I would like to share my experience.

00:00:13.394 --> 00:00:37.273
At my school, pupils have had to leave their phones in their lockers since last year. At first, many protested, and some parents did too: they wanted to be able to reach their children at any time. But after a few weeks, I noticed changes. During break, pupils talk to each other again, play ball or read. In class, they are more focused.

00:00:37.523 --> 00:00:52.942
I'm not saying the phone is the enemy. Used well, it is a wonderful tool for looking something up or recording a presentation. But a twelve-year-old finds it hard to resist notifications — and so do we adults, for that matter.

00:00:53.192 --> 00:01:02.302
In my opinion, school must remain a place where we learn to concentrate and to talk face to face. Phones can wait for the bell at the end of the day.

00:01:02.552 --> 00:01:09.026
Yours faithfully,
Hélène R., Nantes
